1. Definitions
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

"Software" means BlockMinion (formerly distributed as "Minecraft Mod Orchestra"):
the source code, scripts, resources, documentation and build files distributed
under this License by the Licensor, in the form they are distributed.

"Licensor" means the copyright holder named above, and any other copyright holder
who distributes a Contribution under this License.

"You" means the individual or entity exercising rights under this License.

"Derivative Version" means any work based on the Software: a modified copy, a fork,
a translation, a port, a repackaging, a rebranding, or any work that incorporates
all or a substantial part of the Software's code or resources. Independent Content
(below) is not a Derivative Version.

"Independent Content" means anything You create by using the Software as a tool,
including Minecraft mods, their source code, assets, models, textures, animations,
data, configuration and documentation, as well as the output of agents, scripts or
generators that the Software runs on Your behalf. Independent Content is not a
Derivative Version merely because the Software produced, generated, scaffolded,
built, validated or packaged it, even where the Software's templates contributed
boilerplate to it.

"Redistribute" means to give, publish, host, mirror or otherwise make the Software
or a Derivative Version available to anyone else, in source or binary form.

"Software Resale" means any of the following, whether done directly or through an
intermediary, and whether the thing sold is the Software, a Derivative Version, or
a product or service whose main purpose is to deliver the Software or a Derivative
Version:
  (a) selling, licensing or renting copies of the Software or a Derivative Version
      for a fee, a subscription or any other consideration;
  (b) charging a fee for access to, download of, unlocking of, or use of the
      Software or a Derivative Version, including "pro", "premium", "early access"
      or "paid tier" gating of its features;
  (c) renaming, rebranding, re-skinning, obfuscating or lightly modifying the
      Software and doing (a) or (b) with the result;
  (d) bundling the Software or a Derivative Version into a paid product in which
      the Software or Derivative Version is the main thing being paid for.

"Commercial Services" means services You sell to others that are genuinely
distinct from Software Resale: installing, configuring, hosting for a specific
customer, customizing, integrating, extending, troubleshooting, maintaining,
operating, teaching or supporting the Software or a Derivative Version, where the
customer pays for Your work and could have obtained the Software or Derivative
Version itself for free.

"Contribution" means any work of authorship submitted by You to the Licensor for
inclusion in the Software.

"Official Marks" means the names, logos and other brand identifiers of the project
described in TRADEMARKS.md.

